## Non-negotiable requirements

- Work directly on `main`.
- Quality first; then performance, security, and token efficiency.
- Every REST route and client call uses `/api/v1`.
- Next.js login and backend proxy code must never bypass authentication.
- Chatwoot remains removed; runtime code uses the first-party lightweight chat app.
- Production and E2E use real server responses, real seeded database records, and real image assets. Maintained E2E specs must not intercept APIs, fabricate responses, inject fake records, or use data-URL placeholder images.
- Visually inspect maintained pages at mobile, tablet, and desktop sizes for consistent shell, spacing, typography, overflow, loading, error, empty, and seeded-data states.
- Bazel may use NativeLink remote cache. Do not configure a remote executor. Do not commit API keys, cache headers, bearer tokens, certificates, or local secret values.
- Fresh `bazel test //...` success after the final code change is mandatory.
- Push by normal fast-forward only; never force-push.

