## Completed implementation that must not regress

- API paths were migrated to `/api/v1` and deployment/API contracts reject unversioned calls.
- Browser authentication bypasses and backend transport trust issues were hardened.
- Chatwoot was removed and a no-residue contract was added.
- Maintained Playwright CI coverage uses real login, real database seed, real data, and app-shell visual checks.
- Legacy mocked browser contracts were removed from executable E2E coverage.
- Cloud Helm mode requires Secret-backed JWT and gRPC TLS values.
- Cloud gRPC uses mTLS and validates SPIFFE identity.
- Setup is one-time, versioned, token protected, and fail closed.
- Helm pods run non-root with read-only root filesystems, dropped capabilities, runtime-default seccomp, resource limits, and startup/readiness/liveness probes.
- Default-deny network policy selects only release pods and no longer blocks unrelated namespace services such as the Kind PostgreSQL pod.
- Monitoring resources render only when monitoring is enabled.
- PostgreSQL and Valkey images are digest pinned; Kind has a native-platform pull fallback.
- Cloud mesh startup retries brief Valkey connection refusal instead of panicking on its first attempt.
- Kind REST probes have bounded deadlines and connection-refused retries.
- CI uses NativeLink remote cache only; remote execution is disabled.

## Current blocker history and implemented fix

The first complete Kind run passed every cloud/web check, then standalone failed with:

```text
invalid builtin agent authentication configuration: configure OHC_AGENT_TOKEN or OHC_AGENT_SPIFFE_ID
```

The chart was updated with `backend.agentAuth.existingSecret` and projected `OHC_AGENT_TOKEN` from Secret key `agentToken`. A second run then failed with:

```text
invalid builtin agent authentication configuration: OHC_AGENT_AUTH_KEY is required in token mode
```

`src/agents/builtin/auth.rs` requires a separate HMAC-SHA256 verification key of at least 32 bytes. The final implementation now:

- documents Secret keys `agentToken` and `authKey` in `deploy/helm/ohc/values.yaml`;
- requires `backend.agentAuth.existingSecret` in standalone mode;
- rejects inline token/key and unsupported file variables;
- projects `OHC_AGENT_TOKEN` and `OHC_AGENT_AUTH_KEY` from the same Secret;
- generates independent ephemeral token/key material in `deploy/tests/kind_e2e_test.sh`;
- checks both projections in `deploy/tests/e2e_ci_execution_contract_test.sh`.

The fast contract was observed red before implementation and green afterward.

## File responsibility map

- `src/agents/builtin/auth.rs`: source of truth for token/HMAC and SPIFFE authentication requirements.
- `src/server/lib.rs`: server startup, standalone auth initialization, mesh transport retry, HTTP/gRPC listeners.
- `deploy/helm/ohc/values.yaml`: public Helm Secret interfaces and runtime defaults.
- `deploy/helm/ohc/templates/backend-deployment.yaml`: fail-closed validation, Secret projection, security context, probes.
- `deploy/helm/ohc/templates/default-deny-network-policy.yaml`: release-scoped default deny.
- `deploy/tests/kind_e2e_test.sh`: authoritative cloud and standalone disposable-cluster acceptance test.
- `deploy/tests/e2e_ci_execution_contract_test.sh`: fast Helm/E2E/security text contract.
- `deploy/tests/docker_compose_e2e_test.sh`: real container-stack smoke test.
- `deploy/BUILD.bazel`: Kind, Compose, contract, image, and mTLS probe targets.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: hosted contract, Playwright, Kind, Compose, audit, and security jobs.
- `.bazelrc`: local remote-cache-only policy; it must not enable remote execution.
- `src/e2e/BUILD.bazel`: maintained real-stack Playwright shards and coverage gate.
- `src/e2e/login_auth.spec.ts`: real login and denial behavior.
- `src/e2e/real_data_contract.spec.ts`: real database seed/data/image behavior.
- `src/ui/next/src/e2e/app-shell-style.spec.ts`: cross-page visual/shell consistency.
- `.agent/task.tmp`: this handoff and verification ledger.

