## Task 6: push and verify GitHub Actions

- [ ] Fetch and require no unseen upstream commit:

```bash
git fetch origin main
git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD
```

- [ ] Push normally:

```bash
git push origin main
```

- [ ] Verify parity:

```bash
git fetch origin main
git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD
```

Expected: `0 0`.

- [ ] Watch the exact pushed SHA:

```bash
pushed_sha="$(git rev-parse HEAD)"
gh run list --branch main --commit "${pushed_sha}" --limit 10
run_id="$(gh run list --branch main --commit "${pushed_sha}" --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId')"
gh run watch "${run_id}" --exit-status
```

- [ ] On failure:

```bash
gh run view "${run_id}" --log-failed
gh run view "${run_id}" --json jobs --jq '.jobs[] | {name,conclusion,url}'
```

- [ ] Reproduce, add a regression contract, fix without skips/mocks/security weakening, rerun the full local gate, commit, push, and watch the new SHA.
- [ ] Require applicable contract, dependency audit, Bazel, Playwright, Kind, Docker, PostgreSQL security, docs, and release checks to pass. Scheduled/manual-only jobs may legitimately be untriggered; distinguish that from failure.

